# Crew beats: small human moments, most of the log. Idle-friendly beats make an
# absent player's astronaut look good. Each astronaut has a home ship; `same A B`
# beats only happen while someone is visiting in a transfer window.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

card beat_coffee
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 8
once
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} and {B} try to bake bread in the galley oven while the visit lasts. Without gravity it rises in every direction at once and comes out shaped like a lung. They eat all of it, warm, with the lights down, and agree not to describe it to anyone at home.
do bond A B 5

card beat_cards
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 8
once
roles A B
when same A B
text {A} teaches {B} a card game from home across a real galley table, not a screen. By the end of the shift {B} is winning, and the rules have been amended three times.
do bond A B 5

card beat_window
type beat
cat wonder
days 6 10
weight 12
once
roles A B
text {A} and {B} keep a channel open as Earth and the Moon slide into the same frame, each at their own window on their own ship. For a long time the link carries only the hum of two sets of fans. At the shift change {B} sends one photo: the Moon, half lit, over a sliver of Earth.
do bond A B 6

card beat_gym
type beat
cat life
days 3 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when cond B ok
text {A} and {B} share the exercise slot over video, two hours a day so their bones still work at Mars. Whoever hangs up first owes the other a dessert. The sessions keep getting longer.
do bond A B 4
do morale A 2

card beat_zipties
type beat
cat life skill
days 10 39
weight 6
once
roles A B
text After a long debate on the fleet channel, {A} and {B} get all seven ships to agree on which drawer the zip ties live in. It has taken the whole flight so far, and it may be the most important engineering decision made out here.
do bond A B 4

card beat_haircut
type beat
cat life
days 12 39
weight 5
once
roles A B
when same A B
when !fired p_birthday
when bond A B >= 0
when away A
when home B
text {A}, visiting since the last transfer window, cuts {B}'s hair with the vacuum clippers. The result is recorded as "within tolerance". {B} agrees and tips in coffee.
do bond A B 5

card beat_home_msg
type beat
cat human
days 8 22
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} records a message for a school group back home that's been following the fleet. The kids send back forty questions, mostly about the toilet. {A} answers every one.
do morale A 4
do trait A warm 2

card beat_home_msg2
type beat
cat human
days 25 39
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The school group writes again: they've built Mars in the classroom out of papier-mâché and want to know if it's the right red. {A} sends back a photo through the window, unprocessed, and a note: "Close. A bit more butterscotch."
do morale A 4

card beat_shelter_night
type beat
cat life
days 8 39
weight 5
once
roles A B
when var storms >= 1
text {A} and {B} compare storm shelters on video and steal each other's best ideas: one more sleeping spot, a hook for the cards, and a sign, now on every ship, that reads "the Sun is not your friend".
do bond A B 4

card beat_early_watch
type beat
cat wonder
days 1 5
weight 10
once
roles A B
when cond B ok
text {A} and {B} share the night watch over the fleet link. From low orbit Earth fills the window, its dark side strung with cities. {A} holds up a thumb, and the planet spills out around it on every side. They talk about home as if it were down the road. For a few more days, it is.
do bond A B 5

card beat_early_call
type beat
cat human
days 2 5
weight 8
once
roles A B
when cond B ok
text {A} and {B} watch the last top-off tankers come and go from their own windows, a few kilometres apart, and narrate each docking on the fleet channel like a sports commentary. By the third one they have a catchphrase, and by the fourth it has gone fleet-wide.
do bond A B 4

# --- Idle-friendly: only for astronauts whose owner hasn't been in for a while ----
card idle_watch
type beat
cat life
days 4 22
weight 10
once
roles A
when idle A >= 3
when cond A ok
text {A} stands the night watch for the whole fleet so the other six can sleep. Unasked. The watch report is two lines long and perfectly neat.
do morale A 2
do trait A warm 2

card idle_watch2
type beat
cat life
days 23 39
weight 10
once
roles A
when idle A >= 3
when cond A ok
text {A} spends a slow day re-stowing the whole ship to the arrival plan, locker by locker. When the others get to theirs, {A}'s list is already on the fleet channel, with tips.
do morale A 2
do trait A brave 1

card idle_mentor
type beat
cat life
days 6 39
weight 8
once
roles A B
when idle A >= 3
when cond B ok
when is B abort_who
text {A} walks {B} through taking the landing by hand over the link: hold, pick a new spot, commit. Step by step, until {B} can call it without the checklist. {A} logs it as training. It is.
do who abort_who B
do bond B A 6
do trait B brave 2

card idle_spares
type beat
once
cat life
days 13 39
weight 8
roles A
when idle A >= 4
when cond A ok
text {A} inventories the spares locker by hand and finds a scrubber cartridge the manifest says was never loaded. Somebody at Starbase packed a margin and ticked the bag in Sharpie. {A} logs it, with a thank-you in the margin.
do res spares 1

# --- Habits: one clone per astronaut, text from roster.lv `habit` ---------------
# Parked in round 11 while every roster habit is still the placeholder: the
# filler read the same for all seven. Uncomment when real habits arrive.
# card habit_beat
# type beat
# cat life
# each crew
# once
# days 12 36
# weight 2
# roles A
# when cond A ok
# when !flag habit_told
# text On the long shifts, {habit} The other six ships have stopped asking about it, and would notice if it went.
# do set habit_told

# --- Small things carried aboard (round 11): generic, castable to anyone. ---
card hb_watch
type beat
cat life
once
days 12 20
weight 1
roles A
when cond A ok
when is A ow_dose
text {A}'s wristwatch is still on home time. At fleet midnight {A} glances at it and tells the net, "Breakfast at home." The answer comes back the same, from a different ship each time: "Enjoy."
do morale A 1

card hb_card
type beat
cat life
once
days 20 26
weight 1
roles A
when cond A ok
when is A ow_list
text {A} clips a new blank postcard inside the flight-plan binder every page, a different city each time, nothing on the back. The fleet guesses where from. {A} has confirmed one, and won't say which.
do morale A 1

card hb_leaf
type beat
cat life
once
days 26 32
weight 1
roles A
when cond A ok
when is A ow_letter
text A dried leaf in a sleeve rides in {A}'s sleeve pocket, picked up on the walk to the pad. Every few days {A} checks it and reports to the net: "Still green on one side." The ground files it as a status.
do morale A 1

